# Security

Treat uploads, pasted text, filenames, and job IDs as untrusted.

## Uploads and paths

Size limits, MIME/type checks, sanitized filenames, no path traversal, job-scoped temp dirs, delete temps on success **and** failure. Check job ownership before read/download/retry.

## Secrets

No API keys in source, Dockerfiles, logs, or client bundles. Config via environment. Never print env vars that hold credentials.

## Subprocess / FFmpeg

Never build a shell string from user values. Use argument lists (`subprocess.run([exe, ...])`). No `shell=True`, no `os.system`, no `eval`.

```python
# BAD
os.system(f"ffmpeg -i {user_path} {out}")
subprocess.run(f"ffmpeg -i {user_path}", shell=True)

# GOOD
subprocess.run(
    ["ffmpeg", "-i", str(safe_input), str(safe_output)],
    check=True,
    capture_output=True,
)
```

FFmpeg inputs must be paths the job already stored, not raw client strings. Rate-limit public job creation when the app is exposed.
